@startuml
title DRAFT - PackageSubscription business lifecycle
state "Effective" as Active
state "Cancellation pending" as CancelPending
state "Expired / inactive" as Expired
[*] --> Active : registration AND fee collection succeeded
Active --> CancelPending : cancellation accepted
CancelPending --> Expired : current cycle ends
Active --> Active : automatic renewal [eligible, sufficient funds, no cancellation]
Active --> Active : manual re-registration extends from current end [not cancellation pending]
Active --> Expired : cycle ends without successful renewal
Expired --> [*]
note right of CancelPending
  Remains usable until current cycle ends.
  New repeated cancellation request: business error.
  Same-request retry: replay; new repeated request: error.\n  Cancellation accepted before cycle end blocks renewal.\n  Exact acceptance/commit boundary remains detailed design.
end note
note right of Active
  Analytical labels, not final API/DB enums.
  Cycle length in days; insufficient funds => no grace.\n  Applied price snapshot per registration/renewal.\n  Day arithmetic and technical-error retry: OQ-07/09.
  Failed initial collection never enters Effective.
end note
note bottom of Expired
  Preserve subscription history and package definition.
  Grace/recovery/re-registration rules not invented.
end note
@enduml
